WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.830
The Foundation regularly deals with anomalies
of a more sinister nature.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.820
The most frightening among these, of course,
are the ones that stalk and kill Foundation

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:10.820
operatives.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.800
For no clear rhyme or reason, sometimes the
Foundation’s agents and researchers become

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.289
subject to things that seek to entrap and
utterly consume them.

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:23.020
Doctor Elizabeth Graham is one such poor soul.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.810
Nowadays her name is whispered through mess
halls and cubicles, since no one really seems

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.019
to know what happened to her.

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:34.130
One moment she was carrying a stack of files
between two offices.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.680
The next, completely gone.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.250
The Foundation’s security teams couldn’t
figure out what happened to her.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:46.070
The CCTV cameras just showed her blinking
out of existence and the files falling to

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.070
the floor.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.960
Her biometric scanners simply returned a dead
signal.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.960
It seemed that one day, Dr. Graham simply
ceased to exist.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.070
Of course, the Foundation isn’t above keeping
secrets from its own personnel.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.010
Perhaps they did find something.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.930
A series of SCP documents, covered in sand,
suddenly appearing in Graham’s office one

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.590
day neatly stacked and paperclipped.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:14.079
All signed by her in her own handwriting,
and detailing her days spent in a pocket reality

00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:15.260
of some sort.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.920
It wouldn’t be the first time it had happened
- the infamous Red Reality incident with Doctor

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.190
Robert Scranton had already upset researchers,
and there was no reason to alarm them further

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.380
about something they couldn’t change.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:32.369
So Dr. Graham’s papers were covered up and
relegated to long term storage, where they

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:34.240
would likely never be thought of again.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.079
But don’t you wonder?

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:38.400
What happened to Dr. Graham?

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.149
The first thing Doctor Graham felt when she
woke up was confusion.

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:45.979
She didn’t remember falling asleep - in
fact, she didn’t remember much at all.

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:51.130
She had been moving files between two offices
at Site-22 on a normal workday.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:56.119
She’d said hello to some of her coworkers
and had a late lunch before returning to work.

00:01:56.119 --> 00:01:57.319
And then…

00:01:57.319 --> 00:01:58.319
nothing.

00:01:58.319 --> 00:02:00.069
The second thing she felt was fear.

00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:03.159
She looked around and realized she was in
some kind of desert.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:07.149
A bright blue sky was overhead and there seemed
to be a sun.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:09.259
But all around her was sand.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:14.129
Massive sand dunes, flowing sand plains and
even what looked like a sand storm in the

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:15.180
distance.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.870
But all there was, was sand.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.849
Doctor Graham then noticed she was still holding
some things.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:24.040
A small folder, filled with paperclipped documents.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:29.340
Pulling one out, she realized what it was
- a template document for an SCP file, complete

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:34.120
with sections for object class, containment
procedures, and descriptions.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:40.110
This place was obviously not normal - but
she had been anomalously transported to it.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.030
It needed to be documented.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:46.620
There was nothing else to do, so she sat down,
and began to write.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.030
She guessed at a number - who knows what SCP
the Foundation was on now, might as well pick

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.579
something from the middle.

00:02:52.579 --> 00:02:59.049
She scrawled SCP-3890 at the top and bubbled
in Keter for the object class.

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:04.150
The containment procedures were spartan, but
effective - no effective measures of containment

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:09.550
were possible, and she would focus on simply
exploring and finding out what was going on.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.370
Then came the description.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:16.270
No point in sticking to the Foundation’s
signature clinical tone, given the circumstances.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:23.340
It was more important to get the information
down, and so she began to transcribe her thoughts.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:29.220
“SCP-3890 is a potentially extradimensional
or extraterrestrial space which I, Doctor

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:35.720
Elizabeth Graham, was somehow transported
to from Site-22 on 02/17/16.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.409
I am uncertain as to whether I was transported
here due to my involvement with the Foundation.”

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.890
After finishing the paragraph, she picked
herself up off the sand dune she had landed

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.859
on and started to walk in the direction of
the sun.

00:03:47.859 --> 00:03:52.409
She didn’t have much information, and exploring
would be necessary if she were to accurately

00:03:52.409 --> 00:03:53.849
document the anomaly.

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:57.379
It didn’t take long before she came across
something in the distance.

00:03:57.379 --> 00:04:03.079
An old collapsed temple - completely ruined
from the outside, the structure sagging in

00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:04.359
on itself.

00:04:04.359 --> 00:04:07.999
It had the columns and facades of a Roman
building, she noticed.

00:04:07.999 --> 00:04:12.379
Peering inside, it was completely empty except
for more sand.

00:04:12.379 --> 00:04:17.709
In the distance, more ruins were present - some
older, and some more modern looking office

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:18.709
buildings.

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:24.940
“In terms of geography, SCP-3890 takes the
form of a seemingly infinite desert plain,

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.710
with ruins of differing architectural design
poking out through the sand.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:33.210
I have noted the presence of buildings of
modern design, along with what appear to be

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.590
ruins of Ancient Roman and Erikeshan structures.”

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:40.470
She only noticed the first figure when the
sun started to set.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:46.949
As the sky shifted to twilight, she saw a
person walking, casting a long shadow.

00:04:46.949 --> 00:04:50.110
Excitedly, she yelled out - to no response.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:56.490
When she approached, she saw a man in an older
suit, with completely lifeless eyes, stumbling

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:57.750
along.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:02.660
“SCP-3890-1 is my collective designation
for the humanoid entities that wander through

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:03.660
SCP-3890.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:08.680
They do not respond to any stimuli and, as
far as I have been able to tell, simply walk

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.590
around without a specific destination.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:16.690
SCP-3980 are either entities that have been
created to resemble humans but imperfect,

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:22.440
or they are humans who have been mentally
altered in some way to rob them of their faculties.”

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:28.090
There did seem to be some kind of a day night
cycle - and she didn’t feel hungry or thirsty

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.259
at all, though she did feel sleepy.

00:05:31.259 --> 00:05:36.120
After her first day in the desert, Dr. Graham
settled in one of the collapsed ruins, drifting

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.449
off to sleep.

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:40.259
The second document opens much differently.

00:05:40.259 --> 00:05:45.900
This appears to be a document for something
designated SCP-3980-2, Keter.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:51.639
The containment procedures are simply to always,
constantly be on guard for it, whatever it

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:52.639
is.

00:05:52.639 --> 00:05:57.610
If Doctor Graham feels something she is approaching
is not as it appears, she is to immediately

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.610
retreat.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.849
The description is a little clearer.

00:06:00.849 --> 00:06:08.470
“SCP-3890-2 is a living entity of varying
shape and size which resides in SCP-3890.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:14.199
I am uncertain as to whether SCP-3890-2 originates
here or if it was transported here at some

00:06:14.199 --> 00:06:16.569
point in the same way I was.

00:06:16.569 --> 00:06:21.770
From what I have observed of its behaviour,
it appears to be some form of predator.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:25.110
SCP-3890-2 is currently hunting me.”

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.940
“I first encountered the entity shortly
after writing down my initial observations

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.100
of SCP-3890.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:35.400
It snuck up behind me while I was resting
and got me while I wasn't paying attention.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:40.240
I was knocked unconscious by its attack and
woke up several hours later, during the night.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.699
It has attacked me several times since that
first encounter, with several hours between

00:06:44.699 --> 00:06:45.699
each attack.”

00:06:45.699 --> 00:06:48.140
She was caught off-guard by it last night.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:52.240
She hadn’t noticed its presence - it seemed
to be just another building in the far-off

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.180
horizon when she sat down and pulled out her
pencil and paper again.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:00.930
She had started to fill in some more information
about the humanoids: they seemed to continually

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:05.909
walk in circles around some of the ruins,
though it was unclear to her why, or even

00:07:05.909 --> 00:07:08.000
whether they were aware of what they were
doing.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.430
But when she pulled her pencil out - she heard
the buzzing in her head.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:18.280
It was like TV static - initially soft and
low, but then ramping up and quickly becoming

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:21.379
deafening, stifling her ability to think.

00:07:21.379 --> 00:07:23.620
She looked up, and she saw it.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:28.550
For a moment it retained its form as the building
in the horizon, but that quickly changed.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.169
It began to unfold on itself, completely black
on the inside.

00:07:33.169 --> 00:07:38.550
Like a dark paper crane continually folding
and unfolding, stretching and compressing

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.090
in on itself.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:44.349
By the time Doctor Graham got to her feet
and ran away, she began to realize what it

00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:47.949
had done and quickly scrawled it onto the
paper.

00:07:47.949 --> 00:07:52.340
“SCP-3890-2 uses amnesticization as a form
of attack.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:56.879
While it has not injured me physically thus
far, I have lost all memory of significant

00:07:56.879 --> 00:07:59.560
chunks of my childhood and early adulthood.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:03.780
I can no longer recall which high school I
went to, or what my first job was.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:08.699
My current hypothesis is that, as an entity,
it feeds upon memory.”

00:08:08.699 --> 00:08:12.729
At first, Doctor Graham avoided buildings
and stayed to the empty parts of the desert

00:08:12.729 --> 00:08:13.729
while walking.

00:08:13.729 --> 00:08:17.940
But when the creature appeared again, unfolding
out of what seemed to be a piece of paper,

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.819
it became clear what it was: a mimic.

00:08:20.819 --> 00:08:26.490
In the coming hours it would pretend to be
a star, a human, a fly, even a patch of dirt

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:30.580
while trying to make Graham come close enough
to consume her mind.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:34.450
The next document opens in even more dire
circumstances.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:39.320
The containment procedures have shifted drastically
- “containment” now focuses on making

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:44.600
sure that the Mimic does not consume any memories
that Doctor Graham can’t afford to lose.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:49.410
She is to write down all vital memories so
she can recall them if they do get destroyed,

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:53.329
and watch for its presence in all situations
and at all times.

00:08:53.329 --> 00:08:58.830
She writes the document while huddled in a
vault in a bank dropped into SCP-3980, since

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.050
it offers a little security from the creature.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:05.720
But the corpses of a family in the bank imply
something less hopeful.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:10.760
They chose to die by their own hand rather
than let the Mimic get to them.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:15.100
Graham plans to kill anything that tries to
enter the vault to ensure the Mimic doesn’t

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.459
get in, but has bigger problems.

00:09:17.459 --> 00:09:22.019
“I have lost all memories regarding how
I came to be employed by the Foundation.

00:09:22.019 --> 00:09:26.670
I know that I am a Foundation researcher with
Level 3 clearance, but I simply cannot recall

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.160
how I came to be in this position.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:33.110
Many of the SCP objects I worked with are
also missing from my memory.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:37.529
I can tell there is a hole there, but I just
don't know what was there before.”

00:09:37.529 --> 00:09:41.070
Her memories of her own identity have been
obliterated.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:47.490
Who she is, where she’s from, what the Foundation
even is - they have all been taken by the

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:48.490
Mimic.

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:53.089
Without fail, it manages to surprise her and
consume an important memory, then dashing

00:09:53.089 --> 00:09:56.750
away as she tries to figure out what got stolen
from her.

00:09:56.750 --> 00:10:00.190
Something small, like her favorite food or
her childhood bedroom?

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:05.720
Or something foundational and fundamental,
like her name and her sense of self?

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:10.230
And avoiding it isn’t an option - it can
pretend to be any of the single grains of

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:12.410
sand in the boundless desert.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:17.740
And Graham came to that conclusion: this is
an infinite dimension of sand, serving as

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.269
a hunting grounds for the Mimic.

00:10:20.269 --> 00:10:22.490
Of course, it could be anything else, too.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:28.470
A brick, a window, any of the buildings, any
of the mindless wandering people or the clothes

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.380
on Doctor Graham’s back.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.769
Any of them could be the Mimic, and Graham
thought of that too.

00:10:33.769 --> 00:10:37.950
It’s why she hasn’t let go of her knife
in days, even though it’s dripping blood

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:43.389
from examining the corpses of the former victims
of SCP-3980-2.

00:10:43.389 --> 00:10:48.620
Even though she doesn’t need to eat or drink,
there is another concern - sleep.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:53.250
The moment she falls asleep, the Mimic will
no doubt be upon her.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:57.220
She hastily scribbled down a little bit more
onto the paper before trying to rest.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.040
“The sun's going down.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:04.029
I can't allow myself to fall asleep - 3890-2
will come in without a doubt if I do.

00:11:04.029 --> 00:11:08.950
I don't have to eat, I don't have to drink,
but I still have to sleep.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:11.320
This place is designed for the mimics benefit.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:16.260
It can hunt its prey to its heart's content
without them dying of thirst and starvation.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.649
Is this an enclosure, maybe?

00:11:18.649 --> 00:11:19.649
Some kind of sick game?

00:11:19.649 --> 00:11:20.649
My name is Elizabeth Graham.

00:11:20.649 --> 00:11:22.079
My name is Elizabeth Graham.

00:11:22.079 --> 00:11:23.079
My name is Elizabeth Graham.

00:11:23.079 --> 00:11:24.709
I can't forget that now.

00:11:24.709 --> 00:11:26.850
This page is my memory.”

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:32.800
The next words she writes on that paper show
something ominous: She can hear crying outside

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.410
her makeshift shelter.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:36.970
The next document, things have changed.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:41.980
Someone named Tony is mentioned in the containment
procedures, someone Graham trusts to take

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:44.760
watch while she sleeps and watch for the Mimic.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:50.579
The descriptions explain: Tony is a child,
only ten years old, who fell into this dimension

00:11:50.579 --> 00:11:54.490
- the same as Graham - when walking home from
the playground.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:57.899
The Mimic can imitate objects, but it can’t
speak.

00:11:57.899 --> 00:11:59.800
The boy is real.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:04.800
They’ve worked out a rudimentary password
system to confirm each others identities regardless.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:09.660
Graham feels almost hopeful - their chances
of survival have doubled, even though they’re

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:10.880
being hunted.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:15.050
Not for their lives, but for the previous
memories inside their heads.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:17.980
But she’s still worried about other things.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:23.029
If people don’t starve or thirst to death
in SCP-3890, do they age?

00:12:23.029 --> 00:12:26.610
How long have the mindless humanoids been
wandering around?

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:29.779
How long has she been wandering around?

00:12:29.779 --> 00:12:33.560
Though she reminds herself of her training,
she also faces the fact that she might have

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:39.810
been exclusively picked for a past reason:
“I have this memory from my childhood, still.

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:44.670
Everything around it is gone, but it's sort
of floating free, devoid of context.

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:49.620
I'm visiting a woman in a hospital, I think
it's a hospital, and I think it's a woman

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.620
I know.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.620
A close relative?

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.519
My mother or my grandmother, I think.

00:12:53.519 --> 00:12:59.560
And I go to visit her, I'm just a kid, twelve
I think, and she doesn't know who I am.

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:00.560
At all.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:03.339
I don't remember what happened before that
or after.”

00:13:03.339 --> 00:13:07.930
Perhaps the Mimic brought her here because
it knew she would hate having her mind consumed

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:08.930
like this.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:13.910
But that would mean it wasn’t just intelligent
- that it was sadistic and cruel.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:18.120
She noted down she’d ask Tony if he had
a similar experience, and they’d be a little

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.920
closer to working it out.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:24.320
The document is hopeful - Doctor Graham now
has something to believe in.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:29.790
The next document is a complete mess - scribblings
and scrawlings in the margins, and the text

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.410
doesn’t even begin to make any kind of sense.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:37.560
It’s all word salad, the ravings of someone
gone utterly insane.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:41.470
She mentions herself, her own name repeatedly
and constantly.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:47.730
But in between are mentions of Tony, the Foundation,
the Mimic, and everything in between.

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:52.930
Doctor Graham has lost her grip on reality
- that, or whatever wrote this wasn’t Doctor

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.490
Elizabeth Graham.

00:13:54.490 --> 00:14:01.870
The document after that has very simple containment
procedures: she is to kill SCP-3980-2, the

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:02.870
Mimic.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.490
“Description: I woke up this morning.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:05.690
Tony was gone.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.430
He was the Mimic.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.180
It was smarter than I thought, I guess.

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:10.180
I was stupid.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.560
I should have seen this coming, but I was
desperate and it knew it.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:17.829
All it left was some scrawled document and
a hole in my head the shape of my name.”

00:14:17.829 --> 00:14:24.490
The Mimic, disguising itself as a child, has
stolen the last thing she had left: her name.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:29.690
All Graham’s precautions were useless - even
though her name was written down a dozen times

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:32.959
in the last documentation, she cannot remember
it.

00:14:32.959 --> 00:14:37.880
In fact, when she reads it, it immediately
removes itself from her mind again.

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:42.360
Not only has it taken her memory, its taken
her ability to reform them.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:48.510
And the document it left behind is one of
her own - an SCP template, though of course

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:51.570
she doesn’t know what the Foundation is
anymore.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.290
The same document we have seen previously
in the pile.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:59.170
Yes, the Mimic is learning to imitate Graham,
and getting better at it.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:03.540
Maybe that’s why she hasn’t been killed
yet - it’s yet to pin down her thought process

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.710
and is waiting until it has her perfectly
memorized.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:12.440
Not that she would know, given that she’s
forgotten how she even came here or when.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:17.940
But the Mimic made a mistake - it took everything
from her, even her hope.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:21.990
Which has left Doctor Elizabeth Graham a woman
with nothing left to lose.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:26.220
She resolves: she will not get out of SCP-3980.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:30.130
The documents will probably wind up back in
the Foundation’s possession from some testing

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:34.839
with an unrelated anomaly, but she will be
a mindless husk or worse.

00:15:34.839 --> 00:15:36.610
She plans to kill the Mimic.

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:42.420
It’s a cowardly, fearful stalker creature,
and only hunts by pretending to be other things.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:47.380
She knows she can take it in a fight, and
she still has her knife.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.350
The next document is sober.

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:51.990
The object class: Neutralized.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:55.750
Doctor Graham walked boundlessly through the
desert until the Mimic jumped for her.

00:15:55.750 --> 00:16:00.880
It unfolded from a cloud, turning it into
a mass of black origami and lunging for her.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:04.819
It didn’t expect her to turn around and
slash outward with her knife, piercing its

00:16:04.819 --> 00:16:06.240
strange black flesh.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:11.810
It let out a scream, shrank, and Doctor Graham
realized that it could feel pain.

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:16.060
So when it lunged again, she drove her knife
deep into it before pulling back.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:20.779
And she repeated the process until it was
a tiny black mite in the sand, and then she

00:16:20.779 --> 00:16:22.930
crushed it under her heel.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:25.589
It was that easy, that simple.

00:16:25.589 --> 00:16:29.810
But of course, every time it had come close
to her it had taken another bite out of her

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:32.810
mind just as she took another slash at its
form.

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.709
“We opened each other up.

00:16:34.709 --> 00:16:38.870
I filled its body with holes, and it filled
my mind with them.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:40.630
There's not much left of me.”

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:45.560
She curses herself for not having done it
earlier, but maybe there was a reason - she

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.690
can’t remember it anymore.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:51.400
In any case, the Mimic’s dying bites from
her were particularly damaging - the straw

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.350
that broke the camel’s back.

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:56.899
What’s left of Doctor Elizabeth Graham is
falling apart.

00:16:56.899 --> 00:17:01.890
She scribbles things down on the paper while
her mind realizes that she can’t even understand

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:03.670
what she’s writing anymore.

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:06.050
The next document is empty.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:11.070
Not every story with the Foundation’s agents
fighting a monster has a happy ending.

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:17.860
Now go check out “SCP-3001 - Red Reality”
and “SCP-3838 - Nomads of the 4th Dimensional

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:21.350
Steppe” for more other-worldly dimension-related
SCPs!

